{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1764","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller set is; in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (a leaf rule that settles paths and many trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one smaller, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last set found is the answer. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(mean degree d with d² above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the component size in the worst case; the search does not check for task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumDominatingSet()":{"title":"minimumDominatingSet()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller set is; in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","abstract":[],"title":"Covering","url":"\/documentation\/covering"}}}